## SQ-VG-02 | villager walks through a closed Dramatic Doors tall oak door to its bed
> fill 60 -60 -52 64 -57 -48 minecraft:stone hollow
> fill 61 -60 -51 63 -58 -49 minecraft:air
> setblock 62 -60 -52 minecraft:air
> setblock 62 -59 -52 minecraft:air
> setblock 62 -58 -52 minecraft:air
# Dramatic Doors tall doors use third=lower|middle|upper (no half)
> setblock 62 -60 -52 dramaticdoors:tall_oak_door[facing=south,third=lower,open=false]
> setblock 62 -59 -52 dramaticdoors:tall_oak_door[facing=south,third=middle,open=false]
> setblock 62 -58 -52 dramaticdoors:tall_oak_door[facing=south,third=upper,open=false]
> setblock 61 -60 -50 minecraft:red_bed[facing=south,part=foot]
> setblock 61 -60 -49 minecraft:red_bed[facing=south,part=head]
> summon minecraft:villager 62 -60 -58
> time set 13000
pace 0
repeat 60
sleep 1
> execute if block 62 -60 -52 dramaticdoors:tall_oak_door[open=true] run say door_open
end
pace 2
> execute if block 62 -60 -52 dramaticdoors:tall_oak_door run say door_present
> execute positioned 62 -60 -50 if entity @e[type=#zq:villagers,distance=..2]
look door_open lines (1 s samples) may miss a villager passing in under a second; the villager ending inside is the pass
expect \[Server\] door_present
expect Test passed
look the villager ends inside and the door state went open then closed; a tall door placed by setblock may need its upper parts (place it by hand in the client block if the first sample shows a broken door)

