## SQ-VL-01 | villager climbs a ladder to a bed on a platform
# clear the SQ-VG beds and villagers first (they pulled the villager away on 10-31); tag the test villager
> difficulty peaceful
> kill @e[type=#zq:villagers]
> fill 66 -60 -64 76 -53 -56 minecraft:air
> fill 61 -60 -50 61 -60 -49 minecraft:air
> fill 52 -60 -40 52 -60 -39 minecraft:air
> fill 70 -60 -60 70 -55 -60 minecraft:stone
# ladder up to the platform layer (-54): ending at -55 left a one-block step the villager cannot take
> fill 71 -60 -60 71 -54 -60 minecraft:ladder[facing=east]
> fill 66 -54 -64 70 -54 -56 minecraft:stone
> setblock 68 -53 -60 minecraft:red_bed[facing=south,part=foot]
> setblock 68 -53 -59 minecraft:red_bed[facing=south,part=head]
> summon minecraft:villager 76 -60 -60 {Tags:["qvl"]}
> time set 13000
repeat 20
sleep 2
> execute as @e[tag=qvl,limit=1] run data get entity @s Pos
end
look Y rises along x 71 to -53 and the villager reaches the bed (last Pos y about -53)

## SQ-VL-02 | villager climbs down in the morning, no fall damage
> time set 1000
repeat 20
sleep 2
> execute as @e[tag=qvl,limit=1] run data get entity @s Pos
end
reject (?i)fell from a high place|hit the ground too hard
look Y falls step by step in the ladder column, then it walks off at the bottom

## SQ-CS-06 | crop_seasons.json edit + /reload moves wheat (run last: /reload truncates the KubeJS log)
shell python3 -c "import json;p='kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/crop_seasons.json';d=json.load(open(p));b=d['blocks'];b['temperate'].remove('minecraft:wheat');b['cold'].append('minecraft:wheat');json.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)"
> reload
sleep 20
> execute if block 30 -60 30 #creativeengineering:crop_seasons/cold
> execute if block 30 -60 30 #creativeengineering:crop_seasons/temperate
shell cp "$INST/kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/crop_seasons.json" kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/crop_seasons.json
expect Test passed
expect Test failed
look the shell step restored the instance file in srv; /reload again before any later season row
